# Considering the Environment: An Expanded Framework for Teacher Knowledge

**Authors:** Donnelly, Julie, Berry, Landon

## Abstract
The emergence of active learning classrooms (ALCs) on university campuses introduces a need for university teachers to have knowledge of the pedagogical use of physical space. We consider expanding two well-known frameworks for teacher knowledge. Pedagogical content knowledge (PCK) describes teacher knowledge about teaching discipline-specific content. Technological, pedagogical, and content knowledge (TPACK) recognizes digital technology as part of the knowledge base. With increased attention on learning spaces, we propose redefining technology to include non-digital technologies, (e.g. furniture, whiteboards). Further, we add &quot;environment&quot; to the knowledge base to address rhetorical communications from both the physical space and the classroom climate.

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ1220566

